** Deploy WAR to Tomcat Server via pipeline **

	-> Refer - Video 43 of Jenkins  <-
	
	
Step 1) create a Jenkins EC2 instance of Linux / t2.medium

 allow port 8080 to it.

Then,  yum provies java

	- install the java 17 OR 21
	
then install Jenkins on your server


wget -O /etc/yum.repos.d/jenkins.repo \
    https://pkg.jenkins.io/redhat-stable/jenkins.repo
	
rpm --import https://pkg.jenkins.io/redhat-stable/jenkins.io-2023.key

yum install jenkins

systemctl start jenkins

systemctl enable jenkins

 install git 
	 apt install git -y

Also, install maven on the Jenkins Server

and unzip and move to /opt 

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Step 2) create a Tomcat EC2 instance of Linux / t2.micro

 allow port 8080 to it.

Then,  yum provies java

	- install the java 17 OR 21
	
Then , wget https://downloads.apache.org/tomcat/tomcat-9/v9.0.106/bin/apache-tomcat-9.0.106.tar.gz

then, use tar -xzf apache-tomcat-9.0.106 

Then, mv apache-tomcat-9.0.106 tomcat

and move it to /opt 

mv tomcat /opt


Also,

Download and install maven 

and move it to /opt

Then, also install git

yum install git -y

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Step 3) - open tomcat and now we have to modify the below files.

 1st file -  tomcat-users.xml in /opt/tomcat/conf
 
 cd /opt/tomcat/conf
 
 vi  tomcat-users.xml
 
 and in this add the below content 
 
 <role rolename="manager-gui"/>
<role rolename="manager-script"/>
<role rolename="manager-jmx "/>
<role rolename="manager-status"/>
<role rolename="manager-admin"/>
<user username="tomcat" password="12345" roles="manager-gui,manager-script,manager-jmx,manager-status,manager-admin"/>

save it ...

2nd file - context.xml  in /opt/tomcat/webapps/manager/META-INF

cd /opt/tomcat/webapps/manager/META-INF 
vi context.xml

Just uncomment the valve command-

  <!--  <Valve className="org.apache.catalina.valves.RemoteAddrValve"
  allow="127\.\d+\.\d+\.\d+|::1|0:0:0:0:0:0:0:1" /> -->
  
  
  
save it..

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

ste	4) now login to jenkins

install the "Deploy to container" plugin

then, create a pipeline 

and use the below script

pipeline {
    agent any
    stages{
        stage('pull'){
            steps{
                git 'https://github.com/akshaygaikwad21/sonar.git'
            }
        }
        stage('build'){
            steps{
                sh '/opt/maven/bin/mvn clean package'
            }
        }
        stage('deploy'){
            steps{
                deploy adapters: [tomcat9(alternativeDeploymentContext: '', credentialsId: 'tom', path: '', url: 'http://13.201.168.153:8080/')], contextPath: '/', war: '**/*.war'
            }
        }
    }
}



- For stage('deploy') we need to use pipeline syntax .
- in that choose Deploy to container plugin.
- then give mentiones **/*.WAR
- the context path as /
- then, create creditals, 

- give tomcat creditals and its host path 
- add this syntax to stage deploy.

i.e deploy adapters: [tomcat9(alternativeDeploymentContext: '', credentialsId: 'tom', path: '', url: 'http://13.201.168.153:8080/')], contextPath: '/', war: '**/*.war'


